    "content": "<p>If your business is in finance, fintech, or investing, you have probably heard of two names: DIFC in Dubai and ADGM in Abu Dhabi. Both are special financial centres inside the UAE. They look alike on the surface, but they are not the same. Here is a simple way to compare them.</p><h2>What Are DIFC and ADGM?</h2><p>DIFC&nbsp;(Dubai International Financial Centre) is in Dubai and opened in 2004. ADGM&nbsp;(Abu Dhabi Global Market) is on Al Maryah Island in Abu Dhabi and started operating in 2015.</p><p>Both are &quot;onshore&quot; financial centres with their own rules, their own regulator, and their own courts. Cases are heard in English. Both also allow 100% foreign ownership.</p><h2>The Main Differences at a Glance</h2><table><tr><td></td><td><p>DIFC</p></td><td><p>ADGM</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>City</p></td><td><p>Dubai</p></td><td><p>Abu Dhabi</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Regulator</p></td><td><p>DFSA</p></td><td><p>FSRA</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Legal system</p></td><td><p>Its own laws, modelled on English law</p></td><td><p>English common law applied directly</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Known for</p></td><td><p>Banking, insurance, asset management, a large and mature community</p></td><td><p>Fintech, start-ups, funds, family offices</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Cost</p></td><td><p>Often higher</p></td><td><p>Often lower for start-ups, but it depends on your activity</p></td></tr></table><p>Two things stand out. First, ADGM applies English common law directly, while DIFC has built its own set of laws and uses English law to fill gaps. Second, many advisers say ADGM is more budget-friendly for smaller firms. Fees change, so always ask for a current quote.</p><h2>Which One Fits Your Business?</h2><p>DIFC may suit you if:</p><ul><li>Your clients and partners are mostly in Dubai</li><li>You want to be near a big community of banks, insurers, and law firms</li><li>You are building a larger financial business</li></ul><p>ADGM may suit you if:</p><ul><li>You are a start-up or a fintech on a tighter budget</li><li>You like the idea of English common law applied directly</li><li>You are setting up a fund, a holding company, or a family office</li></ul><h2>Do You Really Need a Financial Centre?</h2><p>Not always. If you run a trading company, a consultancy, or a typical small business, a regular free zone or a mainland licence can cost much less and work just as well.</p><p>A financial centre is most useful when you need a financial licence, want investors to see a trusted legal setup, or plan to raise money.</p><h2>Is DIFC or ADGM cheaper?</h2><p>Many advisers say ADGM is cheaper for start-ups and holding companies. Costs vary with your licence type, office space, and visas, so compare written quotes.</p><h2>Do both allow 100% foreign ownership?</h2><p>Yes. Both let you own your company fully.</p><h2>Can I work with clients in the rest of the UAE?</h2><p>Usually yes, but the rules depend on your activity and licence. Ask the centre or your adviser before you decide.</p><h2>Which is better for fintech start-ups?</h2><p>Both have programmes for fintech. ADGM is often seen as more start-up friendly, while DIFC offers a larger finance community. Match the choice to your plan.</p><h2>Need More Help Choosing Your UAE Base?</h2><p>Visit<a href=\"https://www.apexchief.com\" class=\"text-[#f7413e] underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">&nbsp;</a><a href=\"https://www.apexchief.com\" class=\"text-[#f7413e] underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apex Chief</a>&nbsp;for clear, practical guides on business and finance in the UAE and the Gulf. Bookmark us and come back for your next read.</p><p>Fees and rules change. Last checked October 2026. Confirm with the official centres before you apply.</p>",
